.\" Man page for mystrncpy
.TH MYSTRNCPY 3 "2026-09-24" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mystrncpy \- copy at most n characters of a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqmystrfunctions.h\(dq
.PP
.BI "int mystrncpy(char *" dest ", const char *" src ", int " n );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mystrncpy()
function copies at most
.I n
characters from the string pointed to by
.I src
into the buffer pointed to by
.IR dest .
If
.I src
is shorter than
.I n
characters, the remaining bytes of
.I dest
up to
.I n
are filled with null bytes.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters copied from
.IR src ,
not counting any padding null bytes.
Returns \-1 if
.I dest
or
.I src
is NULL, or if
.I n
is negative.
.SH NOTES
If
.I src
contains
.I n
or more characters,
.I dest
is
.B not
null-terminated. The caller must add the null byte manually, for example
.IR dest [ n "] = \(aq\e0\(aq."
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mystrcpy (3),
.BR mystrlen (3)
